VALUES (4400093516060125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Basic introduction to linear algebra in the context of Unit 1. Define it, describe key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain What is machine learning in the context of Unit 2. Define it, describe key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain How supervised learning works. Types of Supervised learning in the context of Unit 3. Define it, describe key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain what is unsupervised learning and working of unsupervised learning in the context of Unit 4. Define it, describe key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Basic introduction to linear algebra is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 1”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to Mathematics equations for Machine learning, Matrices, vectors in linear algebra, Unit 1, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Mathematics equations for Machine learning; Matrices; vectors in linear algebra; Unit 1. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** What is machine learning is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 2”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to classification, Machine learning lifecycle, Different applications of ML, Difference between AI and machine learning Machine Learning and deep learning?, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to classification; Machine learning lifecycle; Different applications of ML; Difference between AI and machine learning Machine Learning and deep learning?. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Supervised learning uses labelled examples. Regression predicts numeric targets and classification predicts discrete classes; validation is required to estimate generalization.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Advantage and disadvantage of supervised learning; Regressions- Linear regression; regression trees; on-linear regression and polynomial regression. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Supervised learning uses labelled examples. Regression predicts numeric targets and classification predicts discrete classes; validation is required to estimate generalization.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Types of unsupervised learning; Clustering algorithm k- means and KNN(k-nearest neighbors); Hierarchical clustering; anomaly’s detection. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

