n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Different Image editing tools-Selection tools is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 3”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to Crop and slice tools, Measuring tools, retouching tool, painting tools, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Crop and slice tools; Measuring tools; retouching tool; painting tools. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to Animations is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 4”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to software Interface- Start page, Creating custom workspace layouts, import formats, keyboard shortcuts, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to software Interface- Start page; Creating custom workspace layouts; import formats; keyboard shortcuts. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to actionscript is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 6”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to navigating actionpanel, different actions – stop(), play(), navigating between frames, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to navigating actionpanel; different actions – stop(); play(); navigating between frames. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

